diff --git a/docs/table-of-contents.md b/docs/table-of-contents.md
--- a/docs/table-of-contents.md
+++ b/docs/table-of-contents.md
@@ -354,6 +354,34 @@
 By default, MyST will _remove folder information_ when creating URLs.
 To make your URL match your folder structure (so that `myfolder/myfile.md` becomes `myfolder/myfile/`), see [](#site-url-folders).
 
+### Choose the source directory for folder URLs
+
+With `site.options.folders: true`, set `project.url_root` to omit a source
+container directory from page URLs:
+
+```yaml
+project:
+  url_root: chapters
+  toc:
+    - file: chapters/index.md
+    - file: chapters/intro/reference-frames.md
+site:
+  options:
+    folders: true
+```
+
+The second file is served at `/intro/reference-frames`, rather than
+`/chapters/intro/reference-frames`. Resolve `url_root` relative to the project
+root, independently of the config file's location. It must name an existing
+local directory. Non-index pages outside that directory cause a build error
+when folder URLs are enabled. The explicit TOC's first page remains the site
+home page at `/`.
+
+Omitting `url_root` preserves the existing project-relative folder URLs.
+With `folders: false`, page URLs remain flat. This option does not change
+source lookup, static assets, or build output directories. It is separate from
+`BASE_URL`, which specifies a deployment URL prefix.
+
 (implicit-toc)=
 
